# Extra host paths bound into every CCY session of this project.
# One per line: <host-src>:<container-dst>[:ro|rw]   (default rw)
# `~/` or `$HOME/` may start the host path. Nothing else is expanded.
#
# Read on the HOST at launch. Every line is validated; the host path must
# already exist (start a FUSE mount first). Any problem refuses the launch.
# Opt out for one launch: CCY_NO_PROJECT_MOUNTS=1 ccy
# Details: docs/ccy.md, "Extra Mounts".
#
# This project declares NO extra mounts, and should not. The file is tracked, so
# an entry here is claimed by every clone on every machine — and a host path that
# does not exist refuses the launch. Declare a bind only if provisioning a Fedora
# desktop genuinely needs it; a bind for your own unrelated work belongs in a
# per-launch CCY_EXTRA_MOUNTS export, not in this file.
#
# Example (commented out — uncomment and adapt only if the project needs it):
# ~/mnt/<drive-folder>:/ccy/mnt/<drive-folder>
